Subject: [PATCH] argus: camera: report the identity of each enumerated device

Argus device indexes are compact and must not be inferred from device-tree
module numbers or video-node suffixes. Print the model and unique module
string next to the actual device index in --info output so the launcher can
resolve a physical EDGEDES port using its imx676/imx678 module badge.

This only adds device information; enumeration and capture are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab launcher integration]

diff --git a/argus/apps/camera/modules/Dispatcher.cpp b/argus/apps/camera/modules/Dispatcher.cpp
--- a/argus/apps/camera/modules/Dispatcher.cpp
+++ b/argus/apps/camera/modules/Dispatcher.cpp
@@ -1307,6 +1307,10 @@ bool Dispatcher::getInfo(std::string &info) const
         if (!iCameraProperties)
             ORIGINATE_ERROR("Failed to get ICameraProperties interface");
 
+        stream << "  Model Name: " <<
+            iCameraProperties->getModelName() << std::endl;
+        stream << "  Module String: " <<
+            iCameraProperties->getModuleString() << std::endl;
         stream << "  Max AE Regions: " <<
             iCameraProperties->getMaxAeRegions() << std::endl;
         stream << "  Max AWB Regions: " <<
